  nonce: 2c02  # 2c02
  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). OWNER RULING 2026-10-25 on the cookie mechanism: document.cookie is declared `simultaneous` under browser_storage_read (the medium) AND env_read (may carry a credential) -- the INV-dadu precedent (javascript.yaml:298-306; the AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP comment: 'a second boundary rather than a second label on the row'). Rejected: browser_storage_read minting host_secret for every storage row (the registry refuses it, io_boundary_types.py:344-353, 'sensitivity depends on what is stored'; INV-tutar's 22.9% host-secret precision lesson) and a per-row label (INV-tutar: 'one fact in two homes'). Premise re-check: stdin is ipc_recv / untrusted_input (ADR-0050 :183-184; go os.Stdin, python sys.stdin python.yaml:905-915). argv rows today are all env_read (host_secret only): python sys.argv :1141 and argparse :1134-1135; javascript process.argv :293-294; rust args/args_os :384; haskell getArgs :258; elixir System.argv :245; erlang init:get_argument* :316-317; swift CommandLine.arguments :178-179 (its note says unreachable). No argv row in go, c/cpp, the JVM languages or objc. document.cookie is env_read (javascript.yaml:295-297). Corrections to the PLAN: (1) go has no os.Args row, so the go arm ADDS a row rather than relabelling one; (2) argv's untrusted_input half needs its own second boundary that mints the label -- under the amended ADR-0050 ipc_recv is the wrong medium for argv, so likely a new argv boundary; choose it in the PLAN; both halves therefore depend on WI-rutup (isbefore added); (3) two-label function-kind argv rows make WI-mozig's defect live, so WI-mozig lands first (isbefore added). P3 kept."  # 2c02
